  answer="ISO 9001 controls documented information under clause 7.5: creating and updating it with proper identification and approval (7.5.2), then controlling its availability, protection, storage, changes and retention (7.5.3). This covers documents you follow and records that prove what happened, including external documents such as supplier certificates. Clause 7.5 keeps this shape in both ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 9001:2026."
